:: Whitney Post Romance
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<set $daily.whitney.postTied to true>>
<<set $daily.whitney.post to { pose: "", ev: "", res: 0, leashed: $worn.neck.type.includes("leash") }>>
<<attach_leash true>>
Whitney stops you outside a shop and points to a bench beside the entrance. <<He>> guides you over,
loops your leash around the metal arm of the bench, then ties it in a bow you could undo if you really wanted to.
<br><br>
"Wait here," <<he>> says. <<He>> gives the bow a quick pull to check it, then points at the shop window. "Two minutes.
You're not allowed to look."
<br><br>
<<He>> takes a few steps towards the door before turning back. <<He>> looks at the leash again, then at you.
"Don't give me that face. It's a surprise, so sit there and don't talk to strangers. And don't let anyone take you."
<br><br>
Whitney says the last sentence quickly, then clears <<his>> throat and looks towards the shop before reaching for the door.
<br><br>
<<link [[Sit, and be the best-behaved dog on the street|Whitney Post Romance Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "play">><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell Whitney it's a lot, out here|Whitney Post Romance Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "shy">><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Look at the window anyway|Whitney Post Romance Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "peek">><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Wait
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<set _pose to $daily.whitney.post.pose>>
<<set _soft to (C.npc.Whitney.love gte 20 or $whitney_orphanage_special_seen gte 3)>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if !$daily.whitney.post.ev>>
	<<set $daily.whitney.post.ev to ["photo", "helper", "sneer", "mistaken", "quiet"].random()>>
<</if>>
<<switch _pose>>
	<<case "play">>
		You sit upright on the bench and fold your hands neatly in your lap. Whitney stares at you for a second,
		then notices people walking past.
		<br><br>
		"Stop it. People are looking." <<He>> covers <<his>> mouth with one hand, but you can still see <<him>> smiling.
		<br><br>
		"Just... stay there," <<he>> says, pointing at you before hurrying into the shop.
	<<case "shy">>
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
			"C-Can you not leave me like this?" you ask. "Everyone can see."
		<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
			"C-Can you stay?" you ask, glancing at the people passing. "I don't like everyone seeing me tied here."
		<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
			"If you really need me to wait, I will," you say. "But don't leave me here too long."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
			"Could you please not leave me tied here on my own?" you ask. "People keep looking."
		<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
			"I'll wait, but I don't like being tied to a bench where everyone can see me," you say.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Seriously?" you say, looking at the leash. "You're tying me up out here?"
		<<else>>
			"It's a lot," you say. "Out here. In front of everyone."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<if _soft>>
			Whitney looks at you, then at the people moving past the bench.
			<<He>> bends down and pulls a little more leash through the bow so you can shift around without the
			collar pulling against your neck.
			<br><br>
			"Yeah? Huh. Two minutes. I can see the bench from the till."
			<<He>> points through the window to the counter inside. "Wave if you hate it and I'll come out."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> waits until you look towards the counter, then goes inside.
		<<else>>
			"Two minutes," <<he>> says with a shrug. "You'll live."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> opens the shop door, looks back at you once, then goes inside.
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		You lean to one side and try to see through the shop window. Before you can make out what Whitney is doing,
		the door opens again.
		<br><br>
		"I said don't look!" <<He>> comes back, grabs your shoulder, and turns you away from the window.
		Then <<he>> pulls the leash tight and reties it shorter, keeping you close to the bench.<<pain 4>><<gpain>>
		<br><br>
		"Eyes forward. You're a fucking menace." <<He>> goes back inside.
		<br><br>
		You hear the shop door close behind <<him>>.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Post Romance Wait 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Wait 2
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<switch $daily.whitney.post.ev>>
	<<case "photo">>
		<<generate2>><<generate3>>
		A <<person2>><<person>> slows down at the sight of the leash tied to the bench. <<He>> looks at your collar, then at your face,
		before taking a phone from <<his>> pocket.
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> stops a few steps away and raises the phone towards you. Behind <<him>>,
		a <<person3>><<person>> notices what is happening and turns to look as well.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Through the shop window, you see Whitney turn away from the counter. <<He>> looks from the raised phone to you.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Look into the lens|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<trauma 2>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Hide your face|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Wave at the window|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<case "helper">>
		<<generate2>>
		A <<person2>><<person>> slows down beside the bench. <<He>> follows the leash from your collar to the bow around the bench,
		then stops in front of you.
		<br><br>
		"Hey. Are you okay? Is somebody making you do this?"
		<<He>> bends towards the knot and puts a hand near it, but waits for your answer before touching it.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Tell <<him>> you're fine|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Let <<him>> try the bow|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Call for Whitney|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gstress>>
	<<case "sneer">>
		<<generate2>><<generate3>>
		A <<person2>><<person>> and a <<person3>><<person>> on the next bench notice the leash.
		The <<person2>><<person>> points at you and says loudly, "Walkies?"
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> laughs. "Who's a good <<girl stranger>>?"
		<br><br>
		The two of them keep watching instead of going back to their conversation.
		The <<person2>><<person>> raises <<his>> eyebrows at you, waiting to see whether you will answer.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Ignore them|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Answer back|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<case "mistaken">>
		<<generate2>><<generate3>>
		A <<person2>><<person>> and a <<person3>><<person>> walk past together and slow down beside the bench.
		The <<person2>><<person>> looks at your collar, follows the leash to the bow, then looks back at you.
		<br><br>
		"Waiting for your owner?" <<he>> asks with a smile.
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> looks at the bow and laughs. "<<pShe stranger>><<pverb "'s" "'ve" stranger>> even been told to stay."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Play along|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<sub 1>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Correct them|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<default>>
		You wait on the bench while people pass along the pavement. After a while, you turn towards the shop window.
		<br><br>
		Whitney is standing beside a display rack with something in <<his>> hands. <<Hes>> already looking at you.
		<br><br>
		When <<he>> notices you looking back, <<he>> turns towards the rack and pushes <<his>> hair away from <<his>> face.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Wave|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Pretend not to have seen|Whitney Post Romance Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<</switch>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Return
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>><<set _post to $daily.whitney.post ?? {}>>
<<set _ev to _post.ev>><<set _res to _post.res>><<set _pose to _post.pose>>
<<set _soft to (C.npc.Whitney.love gte 20 or $whitney_orphanage_special_seen gte 3)>>
<<set _hard to (C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15)>>
<<speechresolve>><<person1>>
<<switch _ev>>
	<<case "photo">>
		The shop door opens while the <<person2>><<persons>> still holding up the phone.
		Whitney steps outside and walks straight across the pavement to stand beside the stranger.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>"Give me the phone and delete it. Now. In front of me." <<He>> holds out <<his>> hand.
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> looks at Whitney, then at the leash tied to the bench.
		<<He>> unlocks the phone, deletes the picture while Whitney watches, and puts the phone away.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Whitney waits until the stranger starts walking away before turning back to you.
		<<if _res is 3>>
			"And you waved." <<He>> points at the shop window, then at you. "At me. In the middle of the street."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> rubs the side of <<his>> neck and looks away. "Which was... fine. Whatever."
		<<elseif _res is 1>>
			"You looked right at that creep. Don't do that for anyone who isn't me."
		<<else>>
			"You covered your face..." <<He>> puts one hand on the back of the bench and leans closer. "Huh. Why the hell should they get a picture, right?!"
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<if _hard>>
			<<He>> takes out <<his>> own phone and raises it.
			"If anyone's getting a picture, it's me."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> waits until you look towards the camera, takes one picture, then lowers the phone.
			<<He>> checks the screen without showing it to you and puts the phone away. <<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glust>>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> takes <<his>> phone halfway out of <<his>> pocket, looks at you, then pushes it back in.
			"I'll take one later. When it's just us."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> turns towards the shop before you can answer.
		<</if>>
	<<case "helper">>
		<<if _res is 2>>
			The <<person2>><<person>> puts both hands on the bow and starts pulling one loop free.
		<<elseif _res is 3>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"W-Whitney!" you call. The shop door bangs open almost at once.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"Whitney!" you call, raising your voice towards the window. "C-Can you come out here?"
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"Whitney, could you come back out?" you call. "Someone's trying to help!"
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Whitney, could you come outside, please?" you call towards the shop.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"Whitney, come out here!" you call. "We need to clear this up."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Whitney! Get out here!" you shout, and the shop door bangs open before you've finished.
			<<else>>
				"Whitney!" you call, and the shop door bangs open before you've finished the second syllable.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<person2>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"I'm okay. Really," you tell <<him>>. The shop door opens before <<he>> can answer.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"I-I'm okay," you say. "Whitney's just inside."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I'm fine," you say. "I agreed to wait here."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Thank you for checking, but I'm all right," you tell <<him>>. "Whitney is inside."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"I'm fine," you say. "You don't need to untie me."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"I'm fine. Mind your own business," you say. The shop door opens before <<he>> can answer.
			<<else>>
				"I'm fine. I chose to wait," you tell <<him>>. The shop door opens before <<he>> can answer.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		Whitney comes straight to the bench and places <<person1>><<his>> hand over the knot before the <<person2>><<person>> can touch it again.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>"Hands off. That's my..." <<He>> stops speaking and looks at you. The <<person2>><<person>> waits.
		Whitney looks back at the stranger. "That's mine to untie. Get lost."
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> looks past Whitney to you. You nod to show you're safe.
		After a moment <<he>> backs away from the bench and continues down the street, still looking back over <<his>> shoulder.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Whitney watches the stranger go before crouching beside the bench and reaching for the knot.
		"Don't let some random creep mess with the leash. If you want out, you tell me."
		<<if _soft>>
			<<He>> keeps <<his>> hand over the knot. "I'm not having some stranger drag you off." <<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "sneer">>
		<<if _res is 2>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"Can you just leave me alone?" you say. The <<person2>><<person>> laughs, and the shop door opens before <<he>> can answer.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"Please leave me alone," you say, keeping your eyes on the pavement.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I don't want to argue with you," you say. "Please just go."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Could you leave me alone, please?" you ask. "This doesn't involve you."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"You've had your laugh," you say. "Now leave me alone."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"At least I know when to shut the fuck up," you say. The <<person3>><<person>> starts to stand, but the shop door opens first.
			<<else>>
				"Better a dog than whatever you are, maggots," you say. The <<person2>><<person>> opens <<his>> mouth to snap back, but the shop door opens first.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			You keep your eyes away from them and refuse to answer. The <<person2>><<person>> repeats the joke more loudly to make you look over,
			while the <<person3>><<person>> laughs and waits for your reaction.
			<br><br>
			Rather than give them one, you turn towards the shop door. <<person1>>Through the glass, you spot Whitney already walking towards it from inside,
			<<his>> attention fixed on the pair beside you.
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> starts to repeat the joke a third time, but the shop door opens before <<he>> can finish.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Whitney stops just outside with a paper bag in <<his>> hand.
		"What was that?" <<He>> looks straight at the pair on the bench. "Say it again!"
		<br><br>
		<<if _hard>>
			Neither of them answers. Whitney walks over and stops in front of them, forcing them to look up at <<him>>.
			<<He>> bends down to say something too quiet for you to make out from the bench.
			<br><br>
			Whatever <<he>> says makes them lose their smiles. The <<person2>><<person>> gets to <<his>> feet first,
			and the <<person3>><<person>> quickly follows.
			<br><br>
			Neither says anything as they leave, and this time they do not look back at you.
		<<else>>
			The pair gets up and walks away. Whitney watches until they are several steps down the pavement.
			"Fuck's sake! Nobody gets to call you that but me."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<person1>><<He>> looks back at you and shifts the paper bag into <<his>> other hand. "Come on, slut. We're leaving." <<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
	<<case "mistaken">>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			You lower your eyes and nod. "I knew it," the <<person2>><<person>> says. "Good pet."
		<<else>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"N-No! Whitney isn't my owner," you say, but the two of them keep looking at the leash.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"N-No..." you say. "Whitney isn't my owner." They look down at the knot, so you look away from it.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"Whitney isn't my owner," you say. "I'm only waiting here because <<person1>><<he>> asked me to."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"No, Whitney isn't my owner," you say. "You've misunderstood."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"Whitney isn't my owner," you say. "The leash doesn't change that."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Owner? Fuck off!" you say. They laugh and point at the bow where your leash is tied.
			<<else>>
				"No! Whitney isn't my owner," you say. The <<person3>><<person>> glances at the leash and raises an eyebrow.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		The shop door opens while the two of them are still beside you. Whitney looks at their faces, then at you.
		"What's going on here?!"
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> points at the leash. "Your pet is very well behaved."
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Whitney's cheeks turn red. <<He>> glances at the shop window, then back at the pair.
		"Goddamn, look at you two. Never seen someone on a leash before? Go find a hobby!"
		<br><br>
		<<He>> waits until the two of them leave before looking at you again.
		<<if _res is 2 and _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
			"You told them I said to wait here?" <<He>> rubs a hand over <<his>> mouth.
			"Don't say that where people can hear you."
			<<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glust>>
		<<elseif _res is 1>>
			"You nodded?" <<He>> looks at the knot, then at you. "Right in front of them?!"
			<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
		<<else>>
			"They didn't buy it," <<he>> says, giving the leash a tug. "Neither do I, with you tied up like that."
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			You wave at the window. Whitney sees you and lifts a hand behind the glass, mouthing "Shut up."
			<<He>> comes out a minute later.
		<<else>>
			You turn away from the window and watch the street. A short while later, the shop door opens behind you.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		Whitney comes out with a paper bag held behind <<his>> leg.
		"Two minutes," <<he>> says, checking <<his>> phone. After a second look at the screen, <<he>> adds, "Make it seven."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<person1>>
<<if _pose is "shy" and _soft>>
	"Tell me if it's too much," <<he>> says. <<He>> scratches the back of <<his>> neck, then reaches towards the knot. "I mean it."
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pose is "play">>
	"And you made it worse by being good at it," <<he>> says, looking at the bench instead of you. "Next time you can be bad at it."
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pose is "peek">>
	"Couldn't even follow one instruction," <<he>> says. <<He>> pulls the leash once, then reaches for the bow. "Nosy dog."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if _ev is "photo" or _ev is "sneer">><<status -3>><<lcool>><</if>>
<<if !["sneer", "quiet"].includes(_ev)>>
	Whitney reaches inside the shop door for the paper bag <<he>> left by the entrance, then returns to the bench.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<He>> crouches beside the bench, unties the leash and gathers it into one hand. With the other, <<he>> holds out the paper bag.
"C'mon, slut, open it. I'm not doing it for you."
<br><br>
<<link [[Open the bag|Whitney Post Romance Gift]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Gift
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
You tip the bag out into your palm. It is a metal tag the size of a bottle cap, cut in the shape of a bone and much thicker than it looks.
One side is stamped with a phone number. The other says IF FOUND, RETURN TO WHITNEY, in letters that slope slightly downhill,
as if the engraving machine at the till had been rushed.
<br><br>
"It's not a present," Whitney says before you can speak. "It's for the collar. In case somebody gets ideas about taking you home.
If they read that, they'll know who you belong to." <<He>> stares hard at the pavement. "And who to ring, so I can go and knock their teeth out."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask Whitney to clip it on for you|Whitney Post Romance Gift 2]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> it's the best present you've ever had|Whitney Post Romance Gift 2]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Point out that the letters are crooked|Whitney Post Romance Gift 2]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Gift 2
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case 1>>
		"Could you clip it on for me?" you ask, holding out the tag.
		Whitney takes the tag, bends the split ring open with a thumbnail, and threads it onto the ring at the front of your collar.
		It takes three tries because <<his>> fingers keep slipping. When the split ring finally closes, the tag settles against your collarbone.
		<br><br>
		"There. Don't lose it," <<he>> says, tugging the collar straight. "And don't you dare take it off."
		<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 3>><<glove>><<glust>>
	<<case 2>>
		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Best present I've ever had," you say, grinning at <<him>>. "Didn't know you had it in you."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			You turn the tag over in your palm. "I think this is the best present I've ever had."
		<<else>>
			"This is the best present I've ever had," you tell <<him>>.
		<</if>>
		"It's not a present," Whitney says again, louder. <<He>> does not take the tag back.
		<br><br>
		"Shut up," <<he>> adds, though you haven't said anything else. <<He>> snatches the tag, clips it to your collar without looking at your face,
		and walks off a few steps with <<his>> ears bright red.
		<<npcincr Whitney love 2>><<glove>>
	<<default>>
		You show <<him>> the engraving. "The letters are crooked."
		"Crooked?" Whitney grabs the tag and squints at it. "The guy said it'd take two minutes! I can't help it if the machine was shit."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> looks at the letters again. "Fine. They're crooked." <<He>> threads it onto your collar and tugs it twice to check it is firm.
		"Say one more word about it and I'll put it on a fucking chain round your ankle instead."
		<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>
The tag taps against the leash clip whenever you move.
<br><br>
<<if $daily.whitney.postOuting>><<link [[Let Whitney lead you in|Town Whitney Shopping Intro]]>><<if !$daily.whitney.post.leashed>><<detach_leash>><</if>><<unset $daily.whitney.post>><<unset $daily.whitney.postOuting>><</link>><<else>><<link [[Let Whitney lead you in|Shopping Centre]]>><<if !$daily.whitney.post.leashed>><<detach_leash>><</if>><<unset $daily.whitney.post>><<endevent>><</link>><</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Hold out the leash handle for Whitney|Whitney Post Romance Reverse]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Romance Reverse
<<effects>><<detach_leash>>
<<speechresolve>>
You unclip the leash from your collar and hold the handle out to Whitney.
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"M-Maybe it's your turn?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You keep holding out the handle but look away from <<him>>. "Maybe... your turn?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"If you want," you say, holding out the handle. "You could try it too."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Your turn," you say, holding the leash out to <<him>>. "Only for a little while."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"You made me do it. So, now... you try."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Your turn, asshole."
<<else>>
	"Your turn."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whitney looks at the handle, then at the people passing the bench. <<He>> does not take it right away.
<<if C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15>>
	"In your fucking dreams."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> reaches for the leash, stops with <<his>> hand halfway there, then looks at you again.
	"You'd drop it. You'd lose me in a minute."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> takes the loose end, wraps it twice around <<his>> wrist, then pushes the handle into your hand.
	"Five seconds. Don't get used to it." <<He>> sits down on the bench, watching the people passing.
<<else>>
	"You can't be serious."
	<br><br>
	Whitney glances at the pavement, wraps the loose leash around <<his>> wrist, then hands you the other end.
	<<He>> sits down on the bench without looking at you.
	<br><br>
	"Like this?" <<He>> looks at the people walking past again. "Fine. Five seconds."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You count aloud while the leash stays loose between you. Whitney keeps <<his>> wrist by <<his>> knee.
When you reach four, <<he>> looks up and reaches for the handle, but starts laughing before <<he>> can take it.
"Okay, okay, I get it. Give it back."
<br><br>
You hand back the handle. Whitney pulls the leash off <<his>> wrist, folds it into <<his>> hand, then holds <<his>> jacket sleeve over <<his>> mouth.
"Don't tell anyone. Don't you dare tell anyone."<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>><<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
<<if $daily.whitney.post.leashed>>
	<<He>> clips the leash back onto your collar.<<attach_leash true>>
<</if>>
<<unset $daily.whitney.post>>
<<if $daily.whitney.postOuting>><<link [[Next|Town Whitney Shopping Intro]]>><<unset $daily.whitney.postOuting>><</link>><<else>><<link [[Next|Shopping Centre]]>><<endevent>><</link>><</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<set $daily.whitney.postTied to true>>
<<set $daily.whitney.post to { pose: "", ev: "", res: 0, leashed: $worn.neck.type.includes("leash") }>>
<<attach_leash true>>
<<generate2>><<generate3>><<person1>>
Whitney stops beside the bike rack instead of taking you through the shopping centre doors.
More people walk past this part of the pavement than the area near the benches.
<br><br>
<<He>> leads you to the rail, wraps your leash around it,
then ties it so you can't walk away without undoing the knot.
<br><br>
Two of <<his>> friends get up from the benches behind <<him>> and come over. A <<person2>><<person>> is already holding a phone, turning it over while <<he>> looks you up and down. A <<person3>><<person>> follows the leash with <<his>> eyes from your collar to the rail,
then glances at the people passing nearby.
<br><br>
The <<person3>><<person>> notices how many people are already staring and starts laughing. <<He>> nudges the <<person2>><<person>> with an elbow and nods at you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Post Bully 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully 2
<<effects>>
A few shoppers notice the group and slow down. One looks from your collar to Whitney, then walks on towards the entrance.
Another keeps glancing back while walking away.
<br><br>
<<person1>>"This is where dogs wait," Whitney says.
<br><br>
<<He>> tugs the leash to test the knot, which pulls the collar tight against your neck.
Then <<he>> lets go and pats your cheek hard enough to sting.
"Twenty minutes. If you're still here when I come out, good dog. If you're not, I'll know, and it'll be worse."
<br><br>
Whitney turns towards <<his>> friends and points at you. "Keep an eye on the <<bitch>>.
If this mutt does anything funny, film it."
<br><br>
The <<person2>><<person>> holds the phone up and points the camera at you.
<<person1>>Whitney looks back at you. "Be a good <<bitch>> and put on a show."
<br><br>
<<link [[Sit where you're told|Whitney Post Bully Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "sit">><<sub 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay on your feet and look at <<him>>|Whitney Post Bully Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "stand">><<def 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<if hasSexStat("exhibitionism", 3)>>
	<<link [[Flaunt it, sit up and pant|Whitney Post Bully Wait]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.pose to "flaunt">><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<pass 5>><</link>><<exhibitionist3>><<gdom>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Whitney Post Bully Wait
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<set _pose to $daily.whitney.post.pose>>
<<speechresolve>><<person1>>
<<if !$daily.whitney.post.ev>>
	<<set $daily.whitney.post.ev to ["photo", "dare", "helper", "commands", "long"].random()>>
	<<if (_pose is "stand" or (_pose is "protest" and (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))) and C.npc.Whitney.love lt random(10, 20)>>
		<<set $daily.whitney.post.extra to true>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<switch _pose>>
	<<case "sit">>
		You lower yourself onto the pavement and sit with your back close to the rail.
		The leash is short, so the collar tugs at your neck whenever you try to shift away from it.
		<br><br>
		Whitney waits until you stop moving, then points down at you and grins.
		"There. Knew you could follow one fucking instruction."
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> takes a picture of you with <<his>> phone while the <<person3>><<person>> laughs.
		Whitney looks at the screen the friend holds out, then turns to the shopping centre.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>"Keep <<phim "Whitney">> there." <<He>> goes inside, and <<his>> friends stay beside the rail.
	<<case "stand">>
		You stay on your feet instead of sitting. Whitney looks down at your legs,
		then at the short leash tied to the rail.
		<br><br>
		<<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>>
			"Fine. Stand." <<He>> grips the leash near your collar and pulls it up until you have to lift your chin.
			"Twenty minutes was the deal. Now it's thirty. Let's see how stubborn you are after standing here that long."
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> laughs and starts a timer on <<his>> phone.
			<br><br>
			<<person1>>Whitney lets go of the leash and points at the friends. "Tell me if this stubborn dog sits down."
		<<else>>
			"Whatever. Stand, then. Twenty minutes is still twenty minutes."
			<<He>> checks the knot again, then points at the ground near the rail. "Don't move from there."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>Whitney goes through the shopping centre doors while <<his>> friends stay behind to watch you.
	<<default>>
		You sit up straight with your hands held in front of you like paws, panting.
		<br><br>
		Whitney starts to turn to the entrance, then stops and looks back at you.
		"Look at this fucking <<slut>>..."
		<br><br>
		Both friends point their phones at you. The <<person2>><<person>> steps several paces to the side
		so the screen shows your collar and the leash tied to the rail.
		<br><br>
		A few shoppers notice the filming and slow down to look. Whitney sees them staring, then pats the top of your head.
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>"Don't stop just because people are watching."
		<<He>> laughs and goes into the shopping centre, leaving <<his>> friends filming you.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Post Bully Wait 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully Wait 2
<<effects>>
<<switch $daily.whitney.post.ev>>
	<<case "photo">>
		<<generate4>><<generate5>>
		Several people glance at you as they pass the rail, but most keep walking.
		Then the <<person2>><<person>> calls out to a <<person4>><<person>> on the pavement. "Hey! Want a picture with Whitney's dog?"
		<br><br>
		The <<person4>><<person>> laughs, takes out a phone, and steps closer. Whitney's friends move aside to give <<him>> a clear view.
		<br><br>
		"Get the collar in," the <<person3>><<person>> says, pointing at your neck. "And the leash. Otherwise nobody's gonna believe this."
		<br><br>
		The <<person4>><<person>> lifts the phone to your face. Behind <<him>>, a <<person5>><<person>> slows down to watch.
		The <<person2>><<person>> leans towards the phone. "Send it round the school when you're done."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Cover your face|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<stress 6>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Look into the lens|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<trauma 3>><<stress 3>><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<gdom>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Tell them to stop|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<stress 3>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>>
	<<case "dare">>
		<<generate4>>
		Whitney's friends start pointing out people passing the entrance. Each time they choose someone,
		they argue quietly about whether that person would come over if challenged.
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> finally waves to a <<person4>><<person>> on the pavement. "Hey! Bet you won't pet the dog."
		<br><br>
		The <<person4>><<person>> looks at you, then at the leash tied to the rail, and laughs before walking over.
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> lifts a phone while the <<person3>><<person>> points at you. The <<person4>><<person>> crouches in front of you,
		one hand resting on <<his>> knee. "Does it bite?"
		<br><br>
		"Why don't you find out?" the <<person3>><<person>> says.
		<br><br>
		The <<person4>><<person>> slowly moves <<his>> hand towards your head while the phone records.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Endure it|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>><<gdom>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Snap at them|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<def 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if Transformations.partActive("traits", "fangs")>>
			<<link [[Bite|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<note "Fangs" "gold">>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<case "helper">>
		<<generate4>>
		A <<person4>><<person>> stops near the rail and looks from your collar to the knot holding the leash in place.
		"Hey. Are you all right?"
		<br><br>
		<<He>> takes a step towards the knot. Before <<he>> can reach it,
		the <<person2>><<person>> moves between the stranger and the rail. "Leave it. The dog likes it. Go on, ask."
		<br><br>
		The <<person4>><<person>> looks around the friend and meets your eyes. Two shoppers behind <<him>> slow down when they realise someone is arguing about you.
		<br><br>
		"Do you want me to untie you?" <<he>> asks.
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> raises <<his>> phone again.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Say you like it|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<stress 6>><<sub 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>><<glust>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Say you want to be let go|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<def 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>>
	<<case "commands">>
		<<generate4>><<generate5>>
		The <<person2>><<person>> crouches in front of you and holds out a hand, while the <<person3>><<person>> stands a few steps back
		with a phone pointed at both of you. A <<person4>><<person>> and a <<person5>><<person>> walking towards the entrance slow down to watch.
		<br><br>
		"Let's see if Whitney trained you properly." <<person2>>The <<person>> moves <<his>> open hand closer to you. "Paw."
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> laughs. "Bet the dog won't even listen."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Give them your hand|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<sub 1>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>><<gdom>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Answer them instead|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<def 1>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Refuse to perform|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<def 1>><<stress 3>><<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>><<pass 25>><<else>><<pass 15>><</if>><</link>><<gstress>>
	<<default>>
		<<generate4>><<generate5>>
		People keep passing you at the rail. Most look once and walk on,
		but a few slow down when they see Whitney's friends filming you.
		<br><br>
		After several minutes the friends stop recording. They stand together, replaying the clips
		and pointing at parts of the screen as they laugh.
		<br><br>
		A <<person4>><<person>> and a <<person5>><<person>> stop nearby. The <<person4>><<person>> points at your leash. "Whose pet is that?"
		<br><br>
		The <<person2>><<person>> answers without lowering the phone. "Owner's shopping."
		<br><br>
		The <<person5>><<person>> laughs, and the two of them walk on towards the entrance, glancing back at your collar.
		You shift beside the rail, but the leash only lets you move a short distance.
		<br><br>
		Twenty minutes pass without any sign of Whitney.<<if $daily.whitney.post.extra>> Then ten more go by.<</if>>
		<br><br>
		The <<person3>><<person>> checks the time and smiles at you. "Guess <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> forgot <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> dog."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Wait quietly|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 1>><<stress 6>><<pass 35>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Test the knot|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 2>><<pass 35>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Call into the shop for Whitney|Whitney Post Bully Return]]>><<set $daily.whitney.post.res to 3>><<stress 3>><<pass 35>><</link>><<gstress>>
<</switch>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully Return
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>><<set _post to $daily.whitney.post ?? {}>>
<<set _ev to _post.ev>><<set _res to _post.res>><<set _pose to _post.pose>><<set _extra to _post.extra>>
<<set _soft to (C.npc.Whitney.love gte 20 or $whitney_orphanage_special_seen gte 3)>>
<<speechresolve>><<fameexhibitionism 5>>
<<switch _ev>>
	<<case "photo">>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			You turn your head away from the phone and hold your forearm across your face.
			The <<person4>><<person>> moves a few steps to the side, looking for a better angle.
			<br><br>
			The <<person3>><<person>> points at the open space beside the rail.
			"Go over there. You'll get the collar in too."
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> does as <<hes>> told and takes four more pictures while you keep your face covered.
			A few people passing the entrance notice the group, look over, then go inside.
		<<elseif _res is 2>>
			You look straight into the phone. The <<person4>><<person>> takes one picture,
			then lowers the phone a little when you keep staring back.
			<br><br>
			Whitney's friends laugh at the <<person4>><<person>> instead. "What? The dog making you nervous now?"
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> takes one more picture without smiling, then puts the phone away and steps back.
		<<else>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"P-Please stop," you say. The <<person4>><<person>> looks at the friends for permission, and the <<person3>><<person>> shrugs.
				The phone keeps filming.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"Please don't take pictures," you say, turning your face away from the phone.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I don't want pictures taken," you say. "Please stop."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Please put the phone away," you say. "I haven't agreed to this."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"Stop taking pictures of me," you say. "Put the phone away."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Put the fucking phone away," you snap. The friends laugh, and the <<person4>><<person>> keeps filming.
			<<else>>
				"Stop," you say. The <<person4>><<person>> looks at the friends for permission, and the <<person3>><<person>> shrugs.
				The phone keeps filming.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> waves at the camera. "Keep going. This mutt gets funnier when the complaining starts."
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> keeps the phone raised while you stay tied beside the rail.
		<</if>>
	<<case "dare">>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			You stay still while the <<person4>><<persons>> hand reaches your head. It pats your hair, then scratches behind your ear
			while Whitney's friends laugh and keep the phone pointed at you.
			<br><br>
			"Good dog," <<he>> says.
			<br><br>
			<<He>> stands up smiling. Before leaving, <<he>> looks at the recording on the <<person2>><<persons>> phone and laughs at the part where you were petted.
		<<elseif _res is 2>>
			<<person4>>You turn your head to the approaching hand and snap your teeth at it.
			<br><br>
			The <<person>> jerks <<his>> hand back and stands so fast that <<he>> nearly bumps into someone passing behind.
			Whitney's friends shout and laugh while the phone keeps recording.
			<br><br>
			"It's only a dog," <<he>> says, rubbing <<his>> hand even though your teeth never touched it.
			<br><br>
			The stranger backs away from the rail, and the <<person3>><<person>> calls after <<person4>><<him>>, "Thought you weren't scared!"
		<<else>>
			You wait until the hand comes close, then bite.
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> shouts and pulls away, holding <<his>> fingers with the other hand.
			Whitney's friends bend over laughing while the phone swings between you and the red marks on the bitten fingers.
			<br><br>
			<<He>> steps backwards and swears at you, but stays near the entrance to show the marks to people passing.
		<</if>>
	<<case "helper">>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"I-I like it," you say, barely getting the words out. The <<person4>><<person>> stares at you,
				then backs away with both hands raised.
				<br><br>
				The <<person2>><<person>> leans in beside your ear. "See? Told you."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"I... I like it," you say, looking away from the <<person4>><<person>>. <<He>> stares at you, then takes a step back.
				<br><br>
				The <<person3>><<person>> laughs. "There. You heard that."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I like it," you say quietly. "You don't need to untie me."
				<br><br>
				The <<person4>><<person>> lowers <<his>> hand from the knot. The <<person2>><<person>> points at you. "See? Good pet."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Thank you for checking, but I want to stay," you say.
				<br><br>
				The <<person4>><<person>> looks confused but steps away from the knot. The <<person3>><<person>> laughs. "Told you."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"I said I'm staying," you tell the <<person4>><<person>>. "Leave the knot alone."
				<br><br>
				<<He>> looks at you for another second, then steps back. The <<person2>><<person>> grins. "Hear that? Trained."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Yeah, I like it. Problem?" you say. The <<person4>><<person>> blinks at you. The <<person3>><<person>> laughs. "Hear that? Good pet."
			<<else>>
				"I like it," you say. The <<person4>><<person>> stares at you, then backs away with both hands raised.
				The <<person2>><<person>> leans in. "See? Told you."
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<person4>>The <<person>> leaves. Whitney's friends watch until <<hes>> out of sight, then the <<person2>><<person>> points the phone at you again.
			"Say it one more time for Whitney."
		<<else>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"I want to go," you say quietly. "Please."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"I want to leave," you say, looking at the knot. "Please untie me."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I don't want to stay here anymore," you say. "Please let me go."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Please untie me," you say. "I want to leave."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"I want to go," you say. "Untie me."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Untie me," you say. "I'm done with this shit."
			<<else>>
				"I want to go," you say.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> reaches for the knot again. Before <<his>> hand gets there,
			the <<person2>><<person>> catches the sleeve and holds on. "<<pShes stranger>> just playing. Stay out of it. Seriously."
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> pulls <<his>> arm free and looks at you. Nobody moves for a few seconds.
			Then <<he>> lowers <<his>> hand. "If you're sure..."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> walks away, looking back once. Whitney's friends wait until <<hes>> gone before laughing.
			"That was pathetic! You nearly got rescued."<<lcool>><<status -5>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "commands">>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			You put your hand into the one held out in front of you.
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> closes <<his>> fingers around your hand and gives it an exaggerated shake while the <<person3>><<person>> records.
			"Good dog. Now speak."
			<br><br>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				You hesitate, then give a small, embarrassed "Woof."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				You look at the phone before giving a quiet, embarrassed "Woof."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				You lower your eyes and give them a soft "Woof."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				You pause, then say, "Woof," while they keep the phone pointed at you.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				You look directly at the camera and bark once.
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				You glare at the phone and bark once, sharply. They laugh harder.
			<<else>>
				You bark once, and the <<person3>><<person>> behind the phone nearly drops it laughing.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> passing behind the camera hears you and looks over.
			The <<person2>><<person>> notices and waves the <<person4>><<person>> closer.
			"See? Whitney actually trained <<phim stranger>>."
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> laughs and walks on towards the entrance.
			"Again," the <<person2>><<person>> says, holding out <<his>> hand a second time.
		<<elseif _res is 2>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				"I-I can speak just fine," you say. "Leave me alone."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"I can talk," you say. "Please stop treating me like that."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"I'd rather answer you normally," you say. "Please leave me alone."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"I'm not doing that," you say. "Please stop."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"I'm not doing tricks for you," you say. "Move."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Go fuck yourself," you say. "There's your trick."
			<<else>>
				"I'm not doing tricks for you," you say.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> laughs and stands up while the phone stays pointed at you.
			"That counts as speaking," the <<person3>><<person>> says. "Whitney can teach the rest later."
		<<else>>
			You keep your hands close to your body and look away from the open hand.
			The <<person2>><<person>> waits, then taps the back of <<his>> hand twice, the way you would call a pet.
			<br><br>
			You still refuse.
			<br><br>
			"Bad dog."
			<br><br>
			The <<person3>><<person>> repeats it for the phone. "Bad dog. Wouldn't do a single trick."
			<br><br>
			The <<person4>><<person>> and the <<person5>><<person>> hear them, look at you, then walk on.
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		<<if _res is 1>>
			<<generate6>>
			You remain beside the rail and wait.
			<br><br>
			People walk around you. A <<person6>><<person>> pushing a pram crosses to the far side of the pavement to avoid the leash.
			Near the entrance, two shoppers stop to look at the knot before going inside.
			<br><br>
			<<person1>>Whitney's friends check the time several times, but make no effort to fetch <<him>>.
		<<elseif _res is 2>>
			You turn to the rail and work at the knot with your fingers. After a few tries you manage to pull one loop partly loose.
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> notices and walks over before you can loosen it further.
			<<He>> takes the loop out of your fingers, pushes it back into place, and pulls the knot tight. "Nice try."
			<br><br>
			The <<person3>><<person>> points a phone at your hands. "Do it again. I want Whitney to see you trying to escape."
			<br><br>
			You move your hand away from the rail.
		<<else>>
			<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
				<<generate6>>"Whitney?" you call. A <<person6>><<person>> inside the shop glances at you through the glass, then at the leash, then looks away.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
				"Whitney?" you call towards the doors. "Can you come back out?"
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				"Whitney, I'm still out here," you call. "Can you come back?"
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"Whitney, could you come outside, please?" you call towards the entrance.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
				"Whitney, get back out here," you call. "You've left me out here too long."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				<<generate6>>"Whitney! Get your ass out here!" you shout. A <<person6>><<person>> inside the shop glances at the leash and immediately looks away.
			<<else>>
				<<generate6>>"Whitney!" you call. A <<person6>><<person>> inside the shop glances at you through the glass, then at the leash, then looks away.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person2>><<person>> cups <<his>> hands around <<his>> mouth and calls towards the doors too. "Your dog misses you!"
			<br><br>
			The <<person3>><<person>> records your face while people near the entrance turn to see who is shouting.
		<</if>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Post Bully Return 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully Return 2
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>><<set _post to $daily.whitney.post ?? {}>>
<<set _ev to _post.ev>><<set _res to _post.res>><<set _pose to _post.pose>><<set _extra to _post.extra>>
<<set _soft to (C.npc.Whitney.love gte 20 or $whitney_orphanage_special_seen gte 3)>>
<<person1>>The shopping centre doors open. Whitney comes outside with a bag on <<his>> arm.
<br><br>
<<He>> does not come straight to the knot. Instead <<he>> joins <<his>> friends, who crowd around <<him>> with their phones.
The <<person2>><<person>> shows a recording while the <<person3>><<person>> points at you and explains what happened.
<br><br>
<<person1>>Whitney watches part of a clip, glances at you, then checks the time on <<his>> phone.
<<if _ev is "long">>
	"Forty minutes! Whoops."
<<elseif _extra>>
	"Thirty minutes! Told you."
<<else>>
	"Twenty on the dot!"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _ev is "photo" and _res is 3>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> tells Whitney you ordered the stranger to stop. Whitney looks from the phone to you.
	"Told <<person4>><<him>> to stop? Who died and made you the boss?"
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> walks over, grips the leash close to your collar, and pulls it shorter until you have to stay near the rail.
	"Smile next time."<<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<stress 6>><<gdom>><<gstress>>
<<elseif _ev is "photo" and _res is 2>>
	The <<person3>><<person>> shows Whitney the pictures. Whitney swipes through them, stops at one,
	then turns the screen slightly towards you without handing the phone back.
	"Look at that face. That's the one I'm keeping."
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> gives the phone back and starts untying the leash. "You can buy a copy. It'll cost ya."<<npcincr Whitney lust 1>><<glust>>
<<elseif _ev is "helper" and _res is 2>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> tells Whitney that you asked the stranger to untie you. Whitney stops beside the rail.
	"Want to be let go?"
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> grips the leash near your collar and pulls upwards. You <<if _pose is "stand">>rise onto your toes<<else>>push yourself up onto your knees<</if>> to ease the pressure on your neck.
	"Think about who decides when you get let go."<<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<pain 2>><<stress 6>><<gdom>><<gpain>><<gstress>>
<<elseif _ev is "helper" and _res is 1>>
	The friends tell Whitney that you said you liked being tied there.
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> laughs, then reaches into the shopping bag and presses a wrapped sweet into your hand.
	"Good dog. Here's your treat."<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<<elseif _ev is "dare" and _res is 3>>
	The <<person4>><<person>> whose fingers you bit is still nearby, checking the marks and swearing.
	<br><br>
	Whitney looks at the bitten hand, then at you, and grabs the rail with one hand while laughing.
	<<if _soft>>
		<<person1>>"Fuck. Fuck, that's good." <<He>> wipes under one eye with <<his>> thumb. "Don't do it to me, though."
	<<else>>
		<br><br>
		<<person1>>"That's my dog." Whitney looks at the stranger again, then lowers <<his>> voice so only you can hear.
		"Try that on me and you'll pay for it."
	<</if>>
	<<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glust>>
<<elseif _ev is "dare" and _res is 1>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> shows Whitney the clip of the stranger touching your head.
	Whitney watches it through once, then looks at you. "Lovely. Look at <<phim "Whitney">> take it."<<npcincr Whitney lust 1>><<glust>>
<<elseif _ev is "commands" and _res is 1>>
	The <<person3>><<person>> shows Whitney the recording. Whitney watches you give your hand to the <<person2>><<person>>, then hears you bark.
	<br><br>
	Whitney lowers the phone and looks at you.
	"You did tricks for them?"
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> grins and hands the phone back. "Next time you do them for me first."<<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<gdom>><<glust>>
<<elseif _ev is "commands" and _res is 2>>
	"They asked for a trick and got told to fuck off," the <<person3>><<person>> says, whether or not those were your exact words.
	<br><br>
	Whitney laughs once, then walks over to you.
	"Still got a mouth on you."
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> grips the leash just below your collar and keeps <<his>> hand there. "Good thing I know where to hold it."<<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<gdom>>
<<elseif _ev is "commands" and _res is 3>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> tells Whitney you refused every command.
	"You wouldn't even give them your hand?"
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> looks at the <<person3>><<person>> who was filming, then back at you. "Waste of a perfectly good video."
<<elseif _ev is "long" and _res is 3>>
	The <<person2>><<person>> tells Whitney how loudly you called for <<nnpc_him "Whitney">>.
	"You called for me?" Whitney asks.
	<br><br>
	<<person1>><<He>> turns towards <<his>> friends and points at you. "Aaaw~ Couldn't wait for your owner to come back?"<<stress 3>><<gstress>>
<<else>>
	<<person1>><<He>> looks at your face, checks the knot, then reaches towards the rail.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Post Bully Return 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Post Bully Return 3
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>><<set _post to $daily.whitney.post ?? {}>>
<<set _ev to _post.ev>><<set _res to _post.res>><<set _pose to _post.pose>><<set _extra to _post.extra>>
<<set _soft to (C.npc.Whitney.love gte 20 or $whitney_orphanage_special_seen gte 3)>>
<<person1>>
<<if _pose is "flaunt">>
	Whitney lowers <<his>> voice so <<his>> friends can't hear. "You enjoyed that. I saw it, and I won't forget."
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pose is "sit">>
	<<He>> pulls once on the leash before touching the knot. "Stayed right where I put you. Good dog."
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pose is "stand">>
	Whitney looks down at your legs, then at you. "Still glad you stood the whole time? Stubborn mutt."
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pose is "protest">>
	"All that complaining," <<he>> says. <<He>> taps the knot with one finger. "And you still waited for me."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set _fame to ((_ev is "photo" and _res isnot 3) or (_ev is "dare" and _res isnot 3) or (_ev is "commands" and _res is 1))>>
<<if _fame>><<status -3>><<lcool>><</if>>
<<He>> unties the leash from the rail, gathers the loose length into one hand,
then <<if _pose isnot "stand">>waits for you to get to your feet before walking<<else>>walks<</if>> towards the shopping centre doors. The first tug makes you step after <<him>>,
and <<his>> friends follow while replaying the clips on their phones.
<<if !_post.leashed>>
	<<He>> stops at the entrance and unclips the leash from your collar.<<detach_leash>>
<</if>>
<<unset $daily.whitney.post>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Shopping Centre]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
